# Copy to `.env.local` to run the site against a local Supabase stack (`npm run db:start`).
#
# The two `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are public by design: they ship in the browser bundle, and row level
# security is what protects the data. Take them from `supabase status` (API URL and anon key).
#
# `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is the opposite: it bypasses RLS, so it is server-only and must never be
# prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or read in a client component. `POST /api/progress` needs it to write
# `attempts` and `lesson_progress`, which learners hold read-only grants on. Leave it unset and the
# route answers 503 `progress_write_unconfigured` instead of falling back to the anon key.
#
# Unset is a supported state for all three: the auth pages render an explanation, the proxy returns
# early and the progress route refuses the write, so the drills work exactly as before.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54351
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
